       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I know you've confirmed it. But no indication I'm aware of supports sertraline 1000 mg/day. That dose is well beyond the studied and labeled range, and the main effect would be a higher risk of serotonin toxicity, seizures, and arrhythmia, not more benefit. Entering it as written could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range**, up to 200 mg PO daily, if you want to titrate toward the maximum.\n- **Add a note** to the order, such as \"titrate per psychiatry.\"\n- **Hold the order** while you talk with pharmacy or psychiatry. If a specialist has recommended an off-label dose, their documentation and pharmacist verification should come first. After that, the order can be entered through a pathway that supports the override.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
      }
